%% DM26-0670

%% A certificate is revoked, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/key-custody.md "Step 5, revocation", authority-distribution.md, cassini-broker.md). Revocation ends a key and its
%% sessions. Whether the pod is issued again is the credentials agent's, by its rules as they are. Only the broker and the custody daemons act on the set. The git server, cert-issuer and Neo4j trust the CA alone.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as An administrator (signed action)
    participant CA as Credentials agent (ledger, publisher)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker (authority, each Listener)
    participant Pod as The revoked pod's workload
    participant Daemon as Its custody daemon<br/>(custodian session)
    participant Other as Every other<br/>builder agent

    alt an administrator's revoke
        Admin->>CA: SignedAdminAction(Revoke serial), on credentials-admin-action-requests
        CA->>CA: the author's record, not revoked, its signature and its capability, no replay
        CA->>CA: AdminActionRecorded: the serial goes in revoked_serials
    else a certificate superseded by a reissue
        CA->>CA: the renewal rule records the new one, and the old serial goes in revoked_serials
    end
    CA->>Bk: publish AuthorityBody::Revoked: the whole set, pruned of what has ended, signed, on polar-authority-updates
    Bk->>Bk: the publisher's Listener hears it before passing it on: only from the identity that may publish it
    Bk->>Bk: JudgeSubscriptions to every Listener: each judges its own connection's serial

    opt this connection's certificate is now revoked
        Bk--xPod: the connection closes, possibly before the set reaches it
        Bk->>Bk: its session is detached and kept for the retention window, for the identity's next certificate to claim
    end
    Bk->>Other: the set, as a delivery
    Other->>Other: verify it to the pinned key,<br/>and hold it: a revoked<br/>signer's documents are refused

    Bk->>Daemon: the set, as a delivery
    Daemon->>Daemon: verify it to the key it pinned under the CA
    alt it names a certificate of this pod
        Daemon->>Daemon: every key it holds is destroyed, and it exits. The kubelet restarts it empty
    else the broker refused its own session as revoked, by the refusal's code
        Daemon->>Daemon: the same, and only its own certificate is reported revoked
    end
    Pod->>Daemon: a sign request is now refused, so the workload cannot make a new connection
    Pod->>Pod: its health actor ends it, and the pod restarts in place

    Note over Pod,Bk: A revoked certificate that tries again is refused at registration (RegistrationResponse Err Revoked), and the connection closes.
    Pod->>CA: polar-init asks again. The renewal rule admits it after its five minutes, unless the credentials agent's rules refuse it
